#!/usr/bin/python3 -I
"""duo-settings-helper: what Duo Settings needs root for.

    duo-settings-helper refresh 60|90           the panels' refresh (the panel
                                                driver's module parameter, kept
                                                in /etc/duo-settings/display.conf;
                                                takes effect when duo-wc starts)
    duo-settings-helper refresh-boot            write the kept refresh to the
                                                driver (duo-panel-refresh.service)
    duo-settings-helper wc-conf KEY VALUE       /etc/duo-wc/duo-wc.conf: hinge_gap
                                                on|off, scale 2|2.25|2.5|2.75|3,
                                                idle_timeout SECONDS, session_lock on
                                                (never off: no app may switch the lock
                                                off), pen_button right_click|off,
                                                pen_dot on|off, pen_input apps|all,
                                                pen_apps "rnote, krita" (app ids,
                                                comma separated); all but scale are
                                                applied live too
    duo-settings-helper pen palm both|panel|off the pen's palm rejection (on both
                                                screens, the pen's screen, off):
                                                /etc/duo2/pen.conf, which duo2-touchd
                                                reads again by itself
    duo-settings-helper pen feel off|ink|pencil|marker|chisel|brush
                                                the pen's writing feel (its haptics
                                                while the tip touches): /etc/duo2/pen.conf,
                                                which duo2-pend reads again by itself
    duo-settings-helper pen strength 1..100     the strength of the pen's haptics
    duo-settings-helper pen click on|off        a click in the pen when its top
                                                button is pressed
    duo-settings-helper pen fw-available        the pen firmware on this phone (JSON: the
                                                newest set in /var/lib/duo2-pen-fw, its
                                                parts and versions; pen-fw.py inspect)
    duo-settings-helper pen fw-update           update the pen with it: pen-fw.py
                                                update --go --until-done (all its checks:
                                                charger, the pen at 50 %, no other device,
                                                newer and Microsoft-signed parts only) as
                                                the transient unit duo2-pen-fw-update,
                                                progress in /run/duo2-pen-fw/status.json
    duo-settings-helper pen fw-stop             stop it (the pen keeps its firmware)
    duo-settings-helper pen charge on|off       charging the pen from the phone (the
                                                Surface Duo 2 Pen Cover): power/'s
                                                duo2-pen-charger on|off, which keeps it
                                                in /etc/duo2/pen-charger and runs the
                                                stock rule
    duo-settings-helper pose dual|span|single DSI-1|single DSI-2
                                                duo-wc's pose, live
    duo-settings-helper laptop on|off|toggle    laptop mode (one panel a desk, the other
                                                a keyboard and a touchpad), live
    duo-settings-helper laptop auto on|off      laptop mode in the laptop posture
    duo-settings-helper laptop keys DSI-1|DSI-2 its keyboard panel when the posture does
                                                not say (duo-wc keeps both settings)
    duo-settings-helper display on_connect ask|desk|mirror
                                                what a display plugged in is used as
    duo-settings-helper display mirror active|both
                                                what a mirroring display shows (the
                                                panel in use, or both; duo-wc keeps them)
    duo-settings-helper restart-display         restart duo-wc (open apps close), once
                                                the user says yes to the shell's
                                                question (duo-wc's confirm: no app
                                                can restart the display by itself)
    duo-settings-helper posed KEY on|off        /etc/duo-posed.conf: enabled,
                                                auto_rotate, auto_pose; then
                                                duo-posed reads it again
    duo-settings-helper posed panels both|left|right
                                                the user's panel choice over the
                                                sensors (duo-posed's panels), and
                                                the pose it means, live
    duo-settings-helper timezone ZONE           e.g. Europe/Budapest
    duo-settings-helper ntp on|off              network time
    duo-settings-helper locale-set LANG REGION DAY
                                                language and formats: LANG and REGION
                                                are generated locales (xx_YY.UTF-8),
                                                DAY auto|mon|sun|sat is the first day
                                                of the week; /etc/locale.conf, applied
                                                when the session restarts
    duo-settings-helper touch-matrix left|right A B C D E F | reset
                                                a panel's libinput calibration
                                                (a udev rule over the shipped one)
    duo-settings-helper battery refresh|clear   the battery usage statistics
                                                (duo2-battery-stats, battery/): a
                                                fresh report now, or clear the
                                                usage history; a signal to the
                                                collector, then waits for its report
                                                and prints it (JSON)

    duo-settings-helper identity                the phone's own identifiers for
                                                Settings > About > Status, as one
                                                JSON line: the serial number (SMBIOS,
                                                root-only) and the modem's IMEIs
                                                (QMI, outside the session's QRTR ban)

    duo-settings-helper geoclue-deny [APP_ID...]
                                                the apps geoclue refuses a position
                                                (Settings > Privacy; desktop ids):
                                                /etc/geoclue/conf.d/91-duo2-apps.conf,
                                                then geoclue starts anew if it runs
    duo-settings-helper sim slots               the SIM slots (JSON: duo2-sim slots:
                                                card, eSIM, active, in use)
    duo-settings-helper sim use 1|2             use the SIM in that slot (1 = the tray,
                                                2 = the eSIM) for calls, messages and
                                                data: duo2-sim use, once the user says
                                                yes to the shell's question (any app
                                                can run this helper); answers JSON
                                                {"ok": ..., "error": ...}

Run by Duo Settings as `sudo -n duo-settings-helper ...`; install-files.sh
puts a sudoers rule for exactly this file in /etc/sudoers.d/duo-settings.
Every argument is checked against a fixed list or pattern: nothing from the
caller reaches a shell or a free path.

Duo Settings is an app like any other (docs/hardware/security.md): duo-wc
refuses it everything but the state on the user's socket. The display
preferences it changes live go through here, as root, to duo-wc's admin
socket, and only those: any app of the user can reach this helper too, so it
offers nothing that unlocks, looks at the screen or switches the lock off.
"""

